.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGEC-SPEC-2026-09-08.md:5:1. **Q1-SCALES** — ACCEPT the proposed normalisations (margin / 20 dB, SE / 4 bit/s/Hz, occupancy / 10 users, angle / 1 rad, times / 120 s, phase / 3); they are scales, not thresholds; sealed with the Q1 schema SHA in spec v1.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGEC-SPEC-2026-09-08.md:8:4. **C3-SET-REPRESENTATION** — set head input = permutation-invariant pooling (sum and max) over the changed users' per-user vectors (their Q1 row for the selected action, their incumbent row, `missing_incumbent`), concatenated with global resource context per affected beam (occupancy before/after, activation change, interference summary, cap margin), padded to |A| ≤ 4 with masks; a two-layer MLP on the pooled vector; anchored zeros by construction (output × 𝟙[|A| ≥ 2]). Shapley for reporting: exact over subsets for |A| ≤ 4.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:6:2. **Executable set-score decomposition (from the review's pass 1(d)).** For a configuration with changed-user set A relative to the anchor reference a⁰ and F = B − η_ref·E: unilateral increments dᵢ = F(aᵢ, a⁰₋ᵢ) − F(a⁰); interaction residual Ψ_A = F(a_A, a⁰₋A) − F(a⁰) − Σᵢ∈A dᵢ. C1(config) = Σᵢ∈A dᵢ (+ Φ), C3(config) = Ψ_A (credited to users by the Shapley allocation of the interaction game; pairs = Ψ/2 each), C2(config) = the declared continuation value excluding the immediate term. Identity: C1 + C3 = F(a_A) − F(a⁰) exactly (KAT). Factor arms: FULL = C1 + C2 + C3; DROP_C1 = C2 + C3; DROP_C2 = C1 + C3; DROP_C3 = C1 + C2 (additive), all in the same selector class and catalogue (stage-4 item 18).
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:10:6. **Information contract for C3 (residual risk 0.90).** Before any successor training, the stages 6–8 contract v1 must state exactly what the learned heads observe and what the coordinator computes (candidate identities, load, shared capacity and interference, activation state, other users' proposed actions or a joint search), with the deployment-capability manifest; retrained ablations are the scientific claim, checkpoint knockouts are reported separately.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:10:5. **Φ semantics.** Because interruption (treatment H) already removes useful time, Φ₁/Φ₂ are declared to price *signalling/QoS preference* (not time, not joules); they are reported alongside the handover rate as co-primary QoS outcomes, and the reward/coordinator use the same event ledger and coefficients.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COUPLED-SOLVE-2026-09-08.md:5:1. **Solver contract.** The capped rate-target map p ← min(cap, Γ·(N₀W + I(p))/ĥ) with `force_cap` rows is a standard interference function (monotone, scalable), so the iteration from p = 0 converges to the unique capped fixed point. Iteration budget raised from 4 096 to 65 536; convergence when the max absolute change ≤ 1e-10 W **or** the max relative change ≤ 1e-9. Convergence is checked on the update, not on a separate residual that treats cap-bound rows differently.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COUPLED-SOLVE-2026-09-08.md:7:3. **KATs.** (a) a 3-user fixture with spectral radius 0.999 converges within budget to the analytic fixed point; (b) a fixture where two users' targets are jointly unattainable certifies `CONVERGED` with both at cap and `rate_target_infeasible`; (c) an injected NaN yields `INVALID` and stops; (d) the real-world rehearsal on the quarantined world 1 evaluates BASE:nearest-eligible without error and reports the certificate distribution over anchors.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGE2-2026-09-08.md:7:3. **World duration / anchors** — **CHANGE**: a unit is not three isolated instants. Each fixed carrier (nearest-eligible, stay-if-possible, random-masked) is rolled for the 30 canonical steps and **every step is a decision instant** (30 anchors per carrier, 90 per world, as in the earlier oracle probe), each with its three-offset forecast steps. If the server-provider rehearsal projects more than 160 core-hours, thin by taking every k-th step with the smallest integer k that brings the projection under budget, chosen from the projection before any unit outcome is opened, and record k in the seal.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGE2-2026-09-08.md:8:4. **Catalogue census** — **CHANGE** for real worlds: the complete Cartesian product of legal assignments is used only when it has ≤ 4 096 configurations (synthetic worlds). Otherwise the union catalogue is the bounded set: (i) every unilateral move of every user to every legal option; (ii) the S0 deployable proposals (top-two per user) and all frozen beam evacuations; (iii) all pairwise joint moves among the top-K = 10 users ranked by nominal unilateral surplus, over all their legal option pairs; (iv) per-active-beam evacuation sets (every user of the beam to its best legal alternative). J1 = the best changed-user-count > 1 configuration in this catalogue; U1 = the best in (i). The catalogue definition and its digest are sealed; the per-world superset check of stage-3 item 10 reports how many legal options fall outside the shortlist.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGE2-2026-09-08.md:9:5. **LC-SRS e_i binding** — **CHANGE**: under the sealed whole-network C1 (which already contains every unilateral bit and joule change of the network), the unilateral externality e_i is inside C1, so the successor C3 target carries **no e_i term**: z₃,ᵢ = Ψ/2 for pairs and the equal-share (Shapley) split of the set interaction for larger sets, with Ψ computed on F = B − η_ref·E per regime (per-cell re-optimisation). This is the round-6 no-double-counting rule; the historical LC-SRS e_i (defined for an own-bits-only C1) is not transferred.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-ENGINE-AUDIT-2026-09-08.md:6:2. **B2 — factor arms cannot measure component marginals (design CHANGE).** The set decoder's score for FULL/DROP arms is the **sum of the declared targets**, not the exact realised objective: S(config) = C1(config) + C2(config) + C3(config), each the declared target in bits computed by the oracle from the same nominal physics (C1 whole-network difference surplus + Φ; C2 three-offset forecasts with −κ; C3 = interaction share per decision item 5 / Shapley for sets). DROP_Cx removes exactly one term inside the **same selector class and the same catalogue**; `DROP_C3` = no interaction term (joint search kept); an additional `UNI` arm = unilateral-only search with all three terms is reported separately (search value ≠ interaction value); `S_UNI` (stage-4 item 11) is the iterated exact-unilateral comparator. The exact-F oracle is a **ceiling arm** (U1/J1/union certificates), never a factor arm. Marginals are measured on the realised pooled endpoint ΣB/ΣE, never on nominal scores. KATs: on a synthetic world with a constructed non-zero interaction, FULL and DROP_C3 select different configurations and the realised marginal equals the hand-computed value; with zero interaction they coincide; DROP_C1/DROP_C2 differ from FULL on fixtures where the dropped term is decisive.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-ENGINE-AUDIT-2026-09-08.md:10:6. **Dead producers.** `assert_calibration_world_separation` runs inside `--manifest` and `--calibrate` (KAT: a deliberately colliding domain pair raises); `resolve_configuration` is the single path every arm uses; `project_three_offsets`/`encode_c2_state` either produce rows that are written to receipts or the C2 schema SHA is **not** stamped into matrix receipts (stamp only where rows exist); `assert_reward_core_identity` runs in every unit's `--dry-run`.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v0-2026-09-08.md:7:2. **Q1 schema (successor, replaces the legacy 228-D):** per action: nominal current fields (SINR margin at rate target, required power / cap, mode SE, occupancy excluding focal, beam-active and satellite-active bits before focal insertion, off-axis angle, D2 remaining time, visibility remaining time, refresh phase), plus the migrated historical tail (previous served association one-hot, previous served load per candidate, previous beam/satellite activity, previous beam max RF / cap), plus `missing_incumbent`; **no** recurrence power, entry-gain ratio or segment age. Exact field list, scales and schema SHA are sealed in v1 of this contract.
